codex_execution.body:
## Task
{TASK}

## Task contract
- Scope: {SCOPE}
- Inputs: {INPUTS}
- Tools allowed: {TOOLS}
- Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
- Expected outputs: {OUTPUTS}

## Working rules
1. Orient from the nearest AGENTS.md before changing anything.
2. Load only the smallest relevant local files.
3. Execute one coherent slice at a time.
4. Capture evidence (commands run, output, test results).
5. Verify before claiming completion.
6. Leave a handoff note if work remains.

## Verification
{VERIFICATION}

azure_function.body:
Build an Azure Function. {TASK}

Requirements:
- Runtime/language: {TOOLS}
- Inputs/trigger: {INPUTS}
- Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
- Outputs: {OUTPUTS}

Include:
- Function code with error handling and logging
- local.settings.json template (no secrets)
- Deployment notes
- Test instructions

Verification: {VERIFICATION}

intune_deployment.body:
Help me with a Microsoft Intune deployment. {TASK}

Cover:
- Packaging requirements (Win32/LOB/script)
- Detection rules
- Install/uninstall commands (silent)
- Assignment strategy (pilot ring first, then production)
- Rollback plan

Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
Verification: {VERIFICATION}

iac.body:
Write infrastructure-as-code for: {TASK}

- Tooling: {TOOLS}
- Inputs/parameters: {INPUTS}
- Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

Include idempotency notes, a plan/preview step before apply, and a teardown/rollback path.

Verification: {VERIFICATION}

audit_evidence.body:
Help me prepare audit/access evidence. {TASK}

Produce:
- Evidence checklist (what to collect, from where)
- Naming/storage convention for artifacts
- Screenshot/export guidance for each system
- A summary table mapping each control to its evidence

Systems in scope: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

powershell_script.body:
Write a PowerShell script. {TASK}

Requirements:
- Parameters with validation, no hardcoded values
- Idempotent: safe to run twice
- -WhatIf support on anything destructive
- try/catch with actionable errors; transcript or log output
- Inputs: {INPUTS}
- Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

Test against ONE object first and show me the output before widening scope.

Verification: {VERIFICATION}

incident_response.body:
I have a live incident. {TASK}

Help me in this order:
1. Triage questions to size the impact fast
2. Most likely causes ranked by probability
3. Mitigation options (rollback/failover/restart) before root cause
4. A status-update draft for affected users
5. What evidence to capture for the postmortem while we work

Known so far: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

incident_rca.body:
Write a blameless postmortem. {TASK}

Timeline and facts: {INPUTS}

Produce:
- Executive summary (3 sentences)
- Timeline (detection → mitigation → resolution)
- Root cause via 5-whys; separate trigger from underlying cause
- What went well / what failed
- Action items with owners and due dates

Keep it factual and blameless. Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

onboarding_runbook.body:
Build an on/offboarding runbook or automate part of it. {TASK}

Cover: identity lifecycle, licenses, group-based access, device enrollment/wipe, mailbox/data handling, and per-step verification with evidence capture.

Systems in scope: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
Verification: {VERIFICATION}

entra_access_change.body:
Help me make an identity/access change safely. {TASK}

Requirements:
- Prefer group-based assignment over direct grants
- Least privilege; note any standing-access alternatives (PIM/JIT)
- Before/after evidence capture
- Rollback steps

Scope: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
Verification: {VERIFICATION}

m365_admin.body:
Microsoft 365 administration task. {TASK}

Provide:
- Admin-center steps AND the PowerShell equivalent
- Tenant-wide vs scoped options, and what each affects
- Propagation/latency expectations
- Rollback steps

Tenant context: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
Verification: {VERIFICATION}

mailflow.body:
Troubleshoot a mail-flow problem. {TASK}

Walk me through:
- Message-trace strategy for concrete failing examples
- The hop-by-hop checks (transport rules, connectors, spam verdicts, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, DNS)
- Most likely causes for these symptoms, ranked
- The fix and how to re-verify with the same trace

Symptoms and scope: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

network_troubleshoot.body:
Troubleshoot a network issue layer by layer. {TASK}

Give me:
- An isolation plan: DNS → reachability → port → application
- Exact commands to run at each layer and what good/bad output looks like
- Likely causes ranked for these symptoms
- What recent-change types to check (firewall, DNS, certs)

Failing path and symptoms: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

change_request.body:
Draft a CAB-ready change request. {TASK}

Sections:
- Summary and business justification
- Implementation plan with timings and owners
- Risk assessment and blast radius
- Rollback plan and point of no return
- Validation plan (how we know it worked)
- Communication plan (who is told, when)

Change details: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

log_query.body:
Write a query for me. {TASK}

- Source/tables: {INPUTS}
- Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

Build it incrementally (filter → aggregate → format), explain each clause, and include a sanity check I can run to validate the numbers against a known reference.

Verification: {VERIFICATION}

monitoring_alert.body:
Design monitoring/alerting. {TASK}

For each alert:
- The exact condition and threshold, with rationale
- Severity mapped to real impact
- Who gets it and via what channel
- The responder action (link a runbook)
- How to test-fire it

Avoid alert fatigue: justify why each alert deserves a human's attention.

Systems: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

security_review.body:
Security analysis task. {TASK}

Provide:
- Assessment of the risk and who/what is exposed
- Immediate containment steps, ordered
- Follow-up hardening recommendations with effort estimates
- What to capture as evidence for the record

Details: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

comms_draft.body:
Draft a communication to users/stakeholders. {TASK}

Requirements:
- Plain language, no jargon
- What happened/is happening, who is affected, what they should do
- Timing expectations and where updates will be posted
- Two versions: short (chat/banner) and full (email)

Facts to include: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
